  "quotes": [
    {
      "block": "原句1",
      "no": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Three Weeks Later",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 14
        },
        {
          "text": "“Two of them,” he says. “That’s twenty in total. Normal for a human in his thirties, right?”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1545
        },
        {
          "text": "“I think so,” I tell him. “Just like your hair and fingernails growing now is normal. And your needing to shave.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1633
        },
        {
          "text": "He nods like he knows this already. Because he does. “It’s just strange, seeing my hair turn gray. Watching it change.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1743
        }
      ],
      "words": 65
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Ninety-seven minutes,” he replies so proudly I nearly burst out laughing",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3603
        },
        {
          "text": "This playful domesticity is more than I ever thought we’d get to have",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4245
        },
        {
          "text": "We don’t know whether he’ll live for another two hundred years, another fifty, or another ten. The same way other people",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4413
        }
      ],
      "words": 60
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Daniel is standing outside the bridal party’s dressing room, looking as on edge",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4731
        },
        {
          "text": "The rest of what he was about to say dies in his throat when he sees me fully, in my burgundy bridesmaid dress and heels",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5396
        },
        {
          "text": "“I’m convinced that any minute now, someone will realize what I used to be and run off screaming.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6959
        },
        {
          "text": "he can still transport himself across small distances",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7333
        }
      ],
      "words": 67
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "When she sees me, she hands the bouquet of lilies she’s carrying to Dr. Cotton, the elderly doctor she works for who wil",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8390
        },
        {
          "text": "“Can confirm,” Asher Lancaster, Liam’s brother and best man, says",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8734
        },
        {
          "text": "A moment later, a string ensemble starts playing Pachelbel’s Canon. That’s our cue. Asher holds out his arm out to me",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9201
        }
      ],
      "words": 68
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“For doing everything you did to make today so wonderful. And for being the best big sister anyone could have asked for.",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9623
        },
        {
          "text": "it feels like an ugly, dark something that I’ve kept buried deep inside rises to the surface and floats away",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9916
        },
        {
          "text": "Or a lot of it does, anyway",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10025
        },
        {
          "text": "If Jess believes so strongly that I’m good enough, maybe over time I’ll eventually believe it, too",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10054
        }
      ],
      "words": 69
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Public speaking still terrifies me as much as it did the day I won back my life and Daniel’s freedom",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 11033
        },
        {
          "text": "On reflex, I reach out to him through our connection that is no longer there, because I need reassurance that I can get ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 11735
        },
        {
          "text": "He gives an infinitesimal nod of his head as if to say You’ve got this",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 11981
        }
      ],
      "words": 69
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I was drawn to you from the moment I laid eyes on you",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 13862
        },
        {
          "text": "In all my years of Reaping, I had never once felt drawn to a person the way I was drawn to you",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 14808
        },
        {
          "text": "In the end, we found each other exactly when we needed to",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 15261
        },
        {
          "text": "And all I had to do was die, I think wryly",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 15320
        },
        {
          "text": "In the end, though",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 15364
        },
        {
          "text": "it was worth it",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 15383
        }
      ],
      "words": 69
    }
  ],
